msgid ""
"Use dry-run jobs to get the usage in resource units and service-side "
"validation a job would incur on a real QPU without spending QPU time."
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dry-run jobs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Dry-run jobs {#dry-run-jobs}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A dry-run job runs your workload through IBM Quantum&reg; Compute Service "
"without using any QPU time. Use a dry-run job to do the following before you"
" commit to a real run:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Get the usage that the job would incur on the real QPU.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Validate the job.** Quantum Compute checks the job's parameters, the same "
"way it does for a real job.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Get the [circuit timing schedule](/guides/qiskit-runtime-circuit-"
"timing)**, if you request it, to debug the job before you run it for real.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Unlike dry-run jobs, local testing (fake backends and [Qiskit "
"Aer](/guides/simulate-with-qiskit-aer)) runs on your own machine and "
"therefore cannot provide usage numbers, service-side validation, or service "
"timing information. To compare the two approaches, see [Mock devices "
"compared to fake backends](#mock-vs-fake).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"- `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.51.0 or later is required for dry-run jobs.\n"
"- Dry-run jobs are available in all regions, and are only available on the Flex, Premium, and On-Prem plans. They are not available on the Open or Pay-As-You-Go plans.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "How it works {#how-it-works}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To run a dry-run job, pass `dry_run=True` to the primitive's `run()` "
"method:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`dry_run` is an argument of the `run()` method (the default is `False`), not"
" a runtime option. It is available to all primitives.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "A dry-run job has the following characteristics:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It runs in IBM Quantum Compute Service in the cloud, not on your machine.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "It uses the calibration data from the real QPU, not just a snapshot. \n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Its results keep the expected schema and follow the expected shape of "
"results from the real QPU, but contain randomized mock data. They are not "
"actual or simulated measurement results, so do not use them to check "
"physical correctness.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Processing happens on the server, so the job might not finish immediately.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Circuit size, shots, and other limits are the same as for any job of that "
"program.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`dry_run=True` also works when the backend is already a mock device.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Read the usage {#read-the-usage}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The usage of a completed dry-run job is the usage the same job would incur "
"on the real QPU, except in rare situations where calibration data changes "
"significantly after the dry-run job and before the job on a real QPU.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`job.usage()` returns the usage in seconds.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`job.metrics()[\"usage\"]` returns the same data together with the usage "
"status.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Dry-run usage is not charged, does not consume your plan allocation, and "
"does not count against any limits.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Do not use job.usage_estimation with dry-run jobs\">\n"
"Do not use `job.usage_estimation` on a dry-run job. Use `job.usage()`.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`job.usage()` returns `0` until the usage calculation is final, so wait for "
"the job to finish before you read it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Circuit timing schedule {#circuit-timing-schedule}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To request the circuit timing schedule, use the same option as for a real "
"job. For full details, see [Visualize circuit timing](/guides/qiskit-"
"runtime-circuit-timing).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Limitations {#limitations}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Job and batch modes only.** Dry-run jobs can only run in [job "
"mode](/guides/execution-modes#job-mode) and [batch mode](/guides/execution-"
"modes#batch-mode).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Flex, Premium, and On-Prem plans only.** Dry-run jobs are not available on"
" the Open or Pay-As-You-Go plans.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Mock devices {#mock-devices}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Mock devices are the implementation behind dry-run jobs. Dry-run jobs hide "
"mock devices by default, but you encounter them in these cases:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Instances configured to access only mock devices.** Example: if you use "
"`service.backend(\"ibm_phoenix\")` to submit a dry-run job on `ibm_phoenix`,"
" but your instance doesn't have access to `ibm_phoenix`,  you will get a "
"`QiskitBackendNotFoundError`. Instead, select the mock device directly with "
"`service.backend(\"mock_phoenix\")`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Compute resources.** Mock devices are hidden by default on the [Compute "
"resources](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers) page. The table on the "
"page has a filter option to include them, but only the Flex, Premium, and "
"On-Prem plans have access to mock devices.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Workloads table.** Jobs from mock devices are hidden by default on the "
"[Workloads](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/workloads) page. The table has a "
"filter option (the funnel icon) to display them.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Python API.** `service.backends()` and `service.jobs()` exclude mock "
"devices unless you call them with `include_mocks=True`. `IBMBackend.is_mock`"
" indicates whether a backend is a mock device. `service.least_busy()` never "
"returns a mock device.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"mock-vs-fake\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Mock devices compared to fake backends {#mock-devices-compared-to-fake-"
"backends}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The names are similar, but a mock device and a [fake "
"backend](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/fake-provider) "
"are different things. A fake backend is a local object in your Python "
"environment. A mock device is a cloud resource in IBM Quantum Compute "
"Service.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | Mock device (for example `mock_phoenix`) | Fake backend (for example `FakeManilaV2`) |\n"
"| --- | --- | --- |\n"
"| What it is | A device in IBM Quantum Compute Service | A Python class in `qiskit_ibm_runtime.fake_provider` |\n"
"| Where it runs | Cloud, in the service | Locally, on your machine |\n"
"| How you get it | `service.backend(\"mock_phoenix\")`, or automatically with `run(..., dry_run=True)` | `from qiskit_ibm_runtime.fake_provider import ...` |\n"
"| Account and instance | Specific plans only (Flex, Premium, or On-Prem) | All instances and plans |\n"
"| Calibration | Live, matches the real device at any time | Fixed snapshot shipped with the installed package |\n"
"| Results | Randomized data with the expected schema. Not a simulation | Noisy simulation that uses the snapshot's noise model |\n"
"| Physically meaningful results | No. Never use them to check correctness | Approximately, within the limits of the noise model |\n"
"| Usage reported | Yes | None |\n"
"| Charged or counted against plan allocation or limits | No | No |\n"
"| Job validation | Done by the service, same as a real job | Limited to what the client checks |\n"
"| Timing schedule | Available on request  | Not available |\n"
"| Execution modes | Job and batch mode only. Sessions are blocked | Session syntax accepted but ignored (local mode has no real sessions or batches) |\n"
"| Completion | Asynchronous, on the server | Runs locally and returns when finished |\n"
"| Shown in platform interface and API lists | Hidden by default (Compute resources, Workloads table, `backends()`, `jobs()`). Opt in to show | Never, because nothing is sent to the service |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "How to choose {#how-to-choose}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To find out **how much usage the job will consume, or whether the service "
"will accept it**, use a dry-run job.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To find out **what the output might look like**, or to work offline, use a "
"fake backend or Aer.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To do both, iterate on circuits and results with a fake backend, then dry-"
"run as the last check before the real QPU.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Common points of confusion {#common-points-of-confusion}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**A mock device is not a simulator.** Its output is random, so sampling a "
"Bell circuit on `mock_phoenix` does not return a Bell distribution. If you "
"want realistic noisy output, use a fake backend.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**A fake backend is not the live device.** Its calibration is a snapshot and"
" might be out of date. A mock device tracks the real calibration, so "
"transpiled circuits and timing match what the QPU sees today.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Neither runs on real hardware.** Neither consumes QPU time, but only a "
"dry-run job goes through the service.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**`usage_estimation` is not the dry-run estimate.** For a dry-run job, "
"`job.usage()` returns the seconds of usage your job would be charged on a "
"real QPU.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Use cases {#use-cases}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Students and courses {#students-and-courses}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An administrator restricts an instance to mock devices only, using the QPU "
"customization toggle when [creating or editing the "
"instance](/guides/instances#add-instance). Students then validate their "
"payloads end-to-end without consuming real QPU time or RUs. Because the "
"instance has access only to mock devices, students select the backend by its"
" mock name:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Project planning {#project-planning}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A team about to start a project dry-runs representative jobs to see the RUs "
"the project needs, before choosing a plan or allocation:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Final check before running on a real QPU {#final-check-before-running-on-a-"
"real-qpu}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Validate parameters and inspect the timing schedule with `dry_run=True`, "
"then drop the argument and run on the real QPU. Nothing else in your code "
"changes:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recommendations\">\n"
"- Test programs on your own machine with [Local testing mode](/guides/local-testing-mode).\n"
"- Learn how [workload usage](/guides/estimate-job-run-time) is measured.\n"
"- Visualize the [circuit timing schedule](/guides/qiskit-runtime-circuit-timing).\n"
"- Understand [resource units](/guides/plans-overview#rus) and the available plans.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
